{
  "version": 1,
  "doc": "Every kind of tile a level can contain. `id` is the number stored in level files and is PERMANENT: never change or reuse one. `key` is its readable name. A kind with a `char` is built into the game (that character is what the game uses for it inside); every other kind has a `behavior` (\"solid\": a block you stand on and are stopped by; \"decor\": a picture behind the player) and the sprite to draw, so a new kind is only an entry here. Ids 0-99: the game's own kinds; 100-999: solid blocks; 1000 and up: decor and anything else. No limit.",
